The long-chunk campaign is closed. Training the compressor on long text chunks (1,024 tokens instead of 256) did not help, and the 2,048-token run is stopped as you asked.

**What I did this wake**
- **Your request ("A — stop the 2048"):** your chat had already cancelled the run at 18:22. I recorded where it stopped and closed it:
  - It reached step 3,561 of 5,208, about 684k of the 1M training documents.
  - It was healthy when stopped.
  - It was never evaluated, so there is no result for 2,048-token chunks.
  - Stopping it saved about 224 GPU-hours.
- **Owner files:** I deleted your request file and the answered question file.
- **Rule file:** I marked the 2,048-token arm "stopped by the owner".
- **Close-out:** I ran the report and the retro, wrote its Lessons, logged a one-line retro, and put the campaign on standby. Later cron wakes now do nothing.

**Result** (judge accuracy, higher is better; 1,500 questions per set; 8 tokens per compressed slot; 1,024-token arm minus the 256-token control, paired on the same questions)

| set | seed 42 | seed 43 |
|---|---|---|
| long text (HotpotQA, one long chunk per question) | −1.1 pt [−3.2, +1.2] | −3.3 pt [−5.4, −1.1] |
| document pages | −6.2 pt [−8.6, −3.9] | −4.3 pt [−6.7, −1.8] |
| photos | +0.3 pt | 0.0 pt |

So keep training on 256-token chunks. Chunk length stays free to choose at inference. In total the campaign used about 26.6 of its 38 GPU-days.

**Two expmon issues, both already reported by earlier wakes, so I only added detail:**
- The retro says the campaign sat idle 85.6 h. In fact the three training runs ran back to back with no gap.
- `expmon display` says the results page has 0 rows, but the page it writes has the full table.

**Your decision:** three small steps, when convenient:
1. Paste `campaign_longchunk/SYNC.md` into `~/.claude/SYNC.md`. Campaign wakes may not write there.
2. Run `expmon campaign disarm` to remove the cron line. Standby already makes those wakes free.
3. Optionally, add the proposed summary in `campaign_longchunk/STATE.md` to `docs/multimodal_results.md`.
